  "hdd_basis": "Existing model drive allowances $1150/$950/$850 in 1980/81/82 plus $150/$100/$100 enclosure, supply, interface and cabling. Early 5 MB subsystem may use an external enclosure; exact OEM remains an engineering qualification assumption. Two floppies retained.",
  "pricing": {
    "dealer_fee": 0.25,
    "fallback_net_contribution_margin": 0.25,
    "comparator_1982_floppy_usd": 3299,
    "comparator_1982_hdd_usd": 4995,
    "balance_formula": "Retail = sqrt(recurring_cost * comparable_price / (1-dealer_fee)). Equalises contribution/net-revenue and discount/comparable-price. 1980\u201381 have no verified comparable basket: use 25% net contribution fallback. 1982 IBM baskets are reference assumptions, with substitute OS qualification in this story."
  },
  "software_timing": "Business Tools and AIONix from May 1980; Abacus 3 added only from November 19 1980. No early native Abacus 2, compatibility card, mouse, networking or later graphics implied. Budget systems retain 16 KiB video and Color II 640x200; network included from May 1981 as in the existing base bundle.",
